  << /ActualText (\240and gas prices by 128\0569\045 in the 12 months to November 2022\056 Many European countries feared a colder\055than\055usual winter combined with the absence of Russian gas supply could further exacerbate an already struggling energy ecosystem\056 Add the lingering shadows of Covid\05519 and its variants and it\047s not surprising that few feel optimistic about what 2023 may bring\056\nLet\047s take a look at what energy sector changemakers will be focusing on this year\056)
     /K [ 13 ]
