  << /ActualText (The northern hemisphere droughts\054 heatwaves and war in Ukraine forced countries to revert to coal and nuclear\055fired generation in 2022 to meet demand\056 While Germany delayed its planned closure of nuclear plants in 2022 in the face of energy security challenges\054 while Japan is planning to restart seven nuclear power plants in 2023\056 With meteorologists predicting a rare third consecutive year of La Ni\361a weather patterns in 2023\054 we should expect more of the same\056\240\nIn spite of these short\055term measures to meet sudden and critical demand\054 renewables are on the rise\056 Global solar capacity is expected to\240)
     /K [ 21 ]
