1560 0 obj
  << /ActualText (\015\240We are part of an energy ecosystem\054 and not one of us can meet 2030 targets\054 enable the energy transition\054 or establish domestic energy security alone\056 Take AI as an example\056 The technology exists to realise the potential role of this game\055changing development\054 but AI\055supporting business practices need to be adopted in order for this to happen\056\240\nThe collaboration doesn\031t stop at business\056 On a different scale\054 we need engagement from consumers\056 DER\054 home battery storage\054 EVs and AI make consumers our partners in the energy transition \055 we need their buy\055in\056 Partner collaboration was a strong theme of the 2022 Enlit conference in Europe\054 so we can expect a strong focus on collaboration in 2023 and beyond\056\nWith war\054 energy scarcity\054 climate catastrophe and economic crisis all casting dark shadows around the globe\054 it can be hard to look positively on the macro environment of the energy industry as we approach 2023\056 But the interplay of these five factors \055 domestic resiliency\054 prosumer tech\054 the shift to renewables\054 increased legislation and partner collaboration \055 represents a tipping point for the global energy industry as we know it\056 We\031re on the brink of a cleaner\054 more cost\055effective and more resilient energy future\054 and perhaps the climate we\031re in right now will serve as the catalyst\056\240\nFor energy retailers\054 the role you play in this tricky\054 eternally disrupted landscape is vital\056 Your work shepherds consumers through the energy transition\056 The best thing you can do to keep ahead of the game and support the critical evolution of the industry is to digitise your systems now\056\240Shall we collaborate\077\240\240)
     /K [ 35 ]
     /P 1561 0 R
     /Pg 1504 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

